# Hardware video decode/encode (Iris v2), loaded by rog5-video.service last,
# after Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, audio and sensors: the video core's apps SMMU
# stream (0x2100) takes a context bank when qcom_iris binds, and a bank taken
# ahead of the PCIe Wi-Fi function broke the Wi-Fi firmware load once (audio,
# r39). Both must bind on every boot with the video DTB (d14): until they do,
# GCC, the RPMh power domains and the interconnects they consume keep
# sync_state() pending (boot-level votes). One module per line, as in
# boot-modules; qcom_iris pulls videodev, v4l2-mem2mem and videobuf2.
videocc_sm8350
qcom_iris
